>Okay, so I'm playing an Elf on PC Nethack, and I often find hidden doors. 
>I open them, go one step in them and then here is nothing.  I search for 
>a few hundred moves, and still nothing.  What's the deal?  Is it a dead 
>end?  Is there a way to go past it?

These little 'closets' are not at all uncommon.  One thing I've
noticed is that they're almost always along the top or bottom walls of
a room, and almost never on the sides.  They can be handy for storing
unused weapons, gems, &c. especially if you have a way to lock the
door.

...
>Also, one time for some strange reason, after a disk access while playing 
>in the middle of a game, PC nethack starts giving me printer errors (I 
>don't have the printer on), so I turn the printer on and retry, and it 
>prints some junk.  Any ideas?  It only happened once.  It could have been 
>a poor disk access.

The only thing I can think of that would cause this is if you typed ^P
(repeat previous message) and the Bios interpreted it as a command to
toggle printer echo.  To fix that, you'd need to set OPTIONS=Rawio in
your nethack.cnf file.  If that's not the case, I can't help you.

